            </profile>
            <profile id="2a2e-8693-7f36-d0b2" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Each wagon has from 5-10 defenders armed with hand weapon, bow and light armour; the defenders of each wagon are a separate unit. May exchange bow for thrusting or throwing spear (free) or halberd (+1 pt), or for crossbow or handgun (+6 pts). Different Weapons. The Wagon Tabor is deployed as one unit and placed first; the wagons are up to 3" apart with the end wagons touching the owning player's table edge; it may not move after deployment. Each undefended wagon at the end of the game gives the opponent +15 Victory points. 0-1 Wagon Tabor, available in Moldavian armies only. (Armies of Chivalry p.49)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
