  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="905c-c519-d4b6-fc47" name="Moldavia &amp; Wallachia (Armies of Chivalry) - List Notes" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF MOLDAVIA &amp; WALLACHIA 1330-1517 (Armies of Chivalry, pp.46-47). Strategist: after choosing sides, the Wallachian or Moldavian general may place one additional terrain feature anywhere on the battlefield outside the enemy deployment zone. Hidden Ambush Force: at the start of deployment the player may set up units with this rule in hiding anywhere on the table that is out of sight and not in the opposing deployment zone, writing down their positions; they deploy at the start of the player's first turn. Allies &amp; Mercenaries entries for Western Men-at-Arms (Superior Men-at-Arms, Free Companies), Crossbowmen (Mercenary Crossbowmen, Italian Condotta), Handgunners and Szekels (Hungary) and Serbian Vlastelas (Ottoman Turks) are documented only.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Moldavia &amp; Wallachia - Moldavia]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: at least 33%
  Infantry: up to 50%, at least 25%
  Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 33%
  The Principality of Moldavia 1359-1517. Characters up to 25%, Cavalry at least 33%, Infantry 25-50%, Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to 33% (includes 0-1 light cannon per 1,000 points). Artillery and Handgunners should be taken only in armies after 1462. Allies: Kingdom of Poland (0-1 Noble who acts as General for the Polish contingent, 0-1 Knights, Retainers, Lithuanian Light Cavalry, Infantry and Handgunners) and Kingdom of Hungary (0-1 Noble, 0-1 Knights, Hungarian/Cuman Cavalry, Szekels, Serbians, Armati, Clipeati, Crossbowmen and Handgunners); Crimean Tartars (Tartar Warriors from the Medieval Russia list) available in Moldavian armies only - all documented only.
[Moldavia &amp; Wallachia - Wallachia]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: at least 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%, at least 25%
  Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 50%
  The Principality of Wallachia 1330-1508. Characters up to 25%, Cavalry at least 25%, Infantry 25-50%, Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to 50% (includes 0-1 light cannon per 1,000 points). Artillery and Handgunners should be taken only in armies after 1448. If Ottoman allies are chosen, the Wallachian army may not include Western Men-at-Arms and Szekels, nor take any Hungarian allies. Allies: Kingdom of Hungary (0-1 Noble who acts as General, 0-2 Knights, Hungarian/Cuman Cavalry, Szekels, Serbians, Armati, Clipeati, Crossbowmen and Handgunners), Ottoman Empire (0-1 Beylerbegh who acts as General, Sipahis, Akincis, 0-1 Janissaries (not Solaks), Volunteers and all Vassals options) and Serbian Vlastelas - documented only.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
